<title>POLAND: POLISH '97 GRAIN SEWN ON 8.7 MLN HE, UP 0.7 PCT.</title>
<headline>POLISH '97 GRAIN SEWN ON 8.7 MLN HE, UP 0.7 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish grain crops this year have been sewn on 8.7 million hectares of land, 64,000 hectares or 0.7 percent more than in 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said in a preliminary estimate on Friday.</p>
<p>GUS said the rapeseed crop had been sewn on 300,900 hectares of land versus 282,600 last year, a 6.5 percent difference.</p>
<p>Sugar beet was seen sewn on 0.4 hectares of land, 8.2 percent less than last year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
